    "result_text": "There is only one test class, and the full suite passes with `BUILD SUCCESS`.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the rule that rejects creating an owner whose normalized telephone is already used by another owner (HTTP 409).\n\n**Change:** added one new small, cohesive class \u2014 `src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/advice/OwnerUniqueTelephoneAdvice.java` \u2014 mirroring the existing `OwnerTelephoneNormalizationAdvice`. It's a `RequestBodyAdvice` scoped to the `addOwner` handler that:\n\n- normalizes the incoming telephone to digits and compares it (digit-normalized on both sides) against every existing owner via `ClinicService.findAllOwners()`,\n- throws a private `DuplicateTelephoneException` on a match, and\n- handles that exception with its own `@ExceptionHandler` returning **409 Conflict**.\n\n**Keeping structural impact low:**\n- No existing method was edited \u2014 the large `OwnerRestControllerV1` and every repository/service interface (and their multiple implementations) are untouched, so I avoided paying the high `WMC_other` of those classes and the file-count multiplier.\n- Only **one file** was touched (created), and each method in it has trivial cyclomatic complexity with almost no surrounding context.\n- `@Order(HIGHEST_PRECEDENCE)` ensures its specific `@ExceptionHandler` wins over the global `Exception.class` handler in `ExceptionControllerAdvice` (the same trick the normalization advice uses), so the 409 isn't swallowed into a 500.\n\nBoth new acceptance tests (`coreRejectsDuplicateTelephone`, `functionalityAllowsDistinctTelephone`) and the full suite pass.",
